  "notes": "Brachiosaurus: a sauropod of the high-browsing kind, 22 m long and over 12 m to the top of its head. The fore legs are longer than the hind, so the back slopes down from tall shoulders, and the neck rises steeply to a small head with a high arch over the nostrils. Warm grey-brown, mottled, paler beneath. Moves in small herds, slowly, and browses tree tops; it hardly minds anyone.",
